------------------------------------------------------------------------
Origin of the driver code
------------------------------------------------------------------------
NiusDisplay's panel drivers are clean-room implementations written from
manufacturer datasheets and controller programming guides. They are not
copied from, and do not derive from, the source of any other display
library.

Where a hardware behaviour is documented only by community reverse
engineering rather than by a datasheet — for example the ST7735 "tab"
variant offsets, the SH1106 132-column window, or the module-specific
colstart/rowstart values in the module database — the observation is
credited in a comment at the point of use, together with the issue or
discussion it came from.

The following projects were studied as prior art for behaviour and for the
catalogue of real-world module quirks. No code was taken from them. Each is
distributed by its own authors under its own license:

  * Adafruit-GFX-Library and Adafruit display drivers — BSD license,
    Copyright Adafruit Industries.
  * TFT_eSPI — FreeBSD (BSD 2-clause) license, Copyright Bodmer.
  * LovyanGFX — FreeBSD (BSD 2-clause) license, Copyright lovyan03.
  * Arduino_GFX — BSD license, Copyright moononournation.
  * u8g2 / U8g2_Arduino — BSD 2-clause license, Copyright olikraus.
  * GxEPD2 — GPL-3.0 license, Copyright Jean-Marc Zingg. Consulted only for
    its published panel/controller compatibility tables, which are factual
    hardware data; no GxEPD2 source was read into, or reproduced in, this
    project.
  * MD_MAX72xx / MD_Parola — LGPL-2.1 license, Copyright majicDesigns.
    Consulted only for its documented FC-16 module wiring variants, which
    are factual hardware data; no source was reproduced.
  * MCUFRIEND_kbv — BSD license, Copyright David Prentice. Consulted for its
    documented controller-ID readback quirks on UNO parallel shields.

